  "date": "05-02",
  "text": "Title: Common knowledge\n\nDefining something as common knowledge can differ based on circumstances because there are variations in what is considered common knowledge amongst \ndifferent groups. The variation can come from the time period, culture, population, class, age, demographic, and other circumstances. \nFor example, the Fifth Amendment to the United States Constitution might be considered common knowledge among people residing in the \nUnited States of a certain age, but cannot be considered common knowledge when considering the general population of other countries.",
